1
00:00:01,540 --> 00:00:06,860
Somewhere in your stores, right now, stock is quietly vanishing.

2
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:09,770
Theft. Till fraud. Miscounts.

3
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:11,040
Short deliveries.

4
00:00:10,910 --> 00:00:12,310
The odd typo.

5
00:00:12,530 --> 00:00:18,850
Up to two percent of sales… usually found weeks later, if at all.

6
00:00:19,410 --> 00:00:22,170
Meet Inventory Sentinel.

7
00:00:22,090 --> 00:00:29,640
It checks every item, in every store, every day, and points your teams to the few places that look wrong.

8
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:31,910
It's plug and play.

9
00:00:31,790 --> 00:00:38,630
Sentinel speaks MCP, so it connects straight to the inventory system you already run.

10
00:00:38,490 --> 00:00:42,680
Add a URL, press sync, and months of history flow in.

11
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:43,950
No migration. No rebuild.

12
00:00:43,870 --> 00:00:49,320
And it's an MCP server too, so your own AI agents can plug right in.

13
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:54,380
Then it learns what normal looks like, with no labels at all.

14
00:00:54,230 --> 00:00:59,310
Sixteen signals, from voided till lines to after-hours scans.

15
00:00:59,210 --> 00:01:08,480
Unsupervised models compete on your own history, and the winner ranks real problems one point seven times better than today's rule.

16
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:12,760
For leadership, it all lands on one screen.

17
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:20,710
Three numbers: the value at risk, the alerts worth a visit this week, and how far it beats the old rule.

18
00:01:20,750 --> 00:01:21,910
Where it happens.

19
00:01:21,950 --> 00:01:23,530
What to work first.

20
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:25,860
No statistics degree required.

21
00:01:26,530 --> 00:01:29,180
Got a tricky question? Just ask.

22
00:01:29,070 --> 00:01:32,460
A team of AI agents splits the work.

23
00:01:32,330 --> 00:01:41,580
One digs through the alerts, another plans investigator hours, all answering from live data, and never inventing a number.

24
00:01:41,710 --> 00:01:44,430
And any change waits for your yes.

25
00:01:44,930 --> 00:01:49,000
Every alert your teams close makes it a little smarter.

26
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:52,500
Inventory Sentinel. Plug it in.

27
00:01:52,450 --> 00:01:56,760
Let it learn. Find the loss… before it's lost.
